{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/552802-selling-humanity-and-blood-smoke","id":552802,"title":"Selling Humanity and Blood & Smoke","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-13T03:18:31-07:00","id":552802,"title":"Selling Humanity and Blood & Smoke","content":"Hey guys<br /> <br /> I'm starting a vampire game tomorrow and one of my more veteran players brought up the alternative rule from the original Vampire book about selling humanity at character creation for 5exp a dot (for up to two dots). Normally I'm quite happy to run this rule but I can't find any reference to it within the updated system, and I'm not sure what exp to give based on the new exp costs.<br /> <br /> Apologies for any inaccuracies, and thanks in advance for your help!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6427-alarura","name":"Alarura","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T03:48:16-07:00","id":552829,"title":"","content":"The rule is gone. And frankly, if this is your first VtR 2.0 game, I would strongly advice against using a house rule for this. In VtR 2.0 it is far easier to lose humanity than in 1.0. Especially players used to the old humanity system might loose 1-2 dots rather quickly. It happened in my first VtR 2.0 session, experienced players quickly lost 2 points of humanity. The hierarchy of sins is vastly different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","name":"Murder-of-Crows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1681_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T05:16:46-07:00","id":552891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-of-Crows</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/552802-selling-humanity-and-blood-smoke?p=552829#post552829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rule is gone. And frankly, if this is your first VtR 2.0 game, I would strongly advice against using a house rule for this. In VtR 2.0 it is far easier to lose humanity than in 1.0. Especially players used to the old humanity system might loose 1-2 dots rather quickly. It happened in my first VtR 2.0 session, experienced players quickly lost 2 points of humanity. The hierarchy of sins is vastly different.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I did not realise they'd changed the hierarchy of sins, I shall have to take a better look. Unfortunately I read though the book pretty well when I first got it but never got around to actually playing it, thanks for the heads up, I'll let them know they can't do it now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6427-alarura","name":"Alarura","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T06:18:06-07:00","id":552922,"title":"","content":"The standard conversion rate is 5 old xp to 1 new Experience, so you wouldn't get much out of the deal anyway, especially since dropping to 6 is what switches on the clan bane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T08:46:31-07:00","id":553099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alarura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/552802-selling-humanity-and-blood-smoke?p=552891#post552891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I did not realise they'd changed the hierarchy of sins, I shall have to take a better look. Unfortunately I read though the book pretty well when I first got it but never got around to actually playing it, thanks for the heads up, I'll let them know they can't do it now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Humanity is a whole different system in B&amp;S. It is a measure of how human you feel. Things that happen to you rather than things you do can effect it. Mind you, your own actions do impact it, but things like being shot, or using disciplines, or joining a covenant can cause humanity loss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T09:45:25-07:00","id":553149,"title":"","content":"Considering also that joining a covenant (ie buying Status dots) is a sin, its a little silly to not check that out as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T11:48:17-07:00","id":553314,"title":"","content":"Yeah, they're called Breaking Points now, instead of Sins because they're pretty explicitly not transgressions against some sort of code, they're just things that remind you you're definitely not human any more. Surviving things that would kill a mortal, depriving someone of conscent with your supernatural powers, joining a Covenant, seeing people you cared about in life die of old age (or on a larger scale, watching civilizations fall), going too long without human contact, all are Breaking Points at various levels. Killing people and other such stuff can also be Breaking Points, but more because they're things most humans don't normally do, rather than because they're a violation of some universal moral standard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T12:30:00-07:00","id":553333,"title":"","content":"It isn't a good rule for 2.0. Any way you look at it the trade in would only be 1 exp. You would start out with a clan bane which doesn't normally happen to allow a character to transition into the life and players to have one less thing to worry about at the start. A veteran player might just assume start with the clan bane though. The question is does the player want to start with less Humanity with all that entails or just have more experience to work with at the start. If it is just about experience then talk to the group. If the veteran is going to take a sort of mentor role then they might not mind if that character starts with a little more experience. Otherwise, all the players could go with having been &quot;around the block&quot; and get an additional 5 experience which would generally amount to around 25 in the first edition. Then any that wants to start with Humanity lower than 7 can certainly still do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T12:35:49-07:00","id":553338,"title":"","content":"I do not normally run Vampire, but I think you could left the rule for price of 5 <b>new</b> XP. That way character could by another Blood Potency dot for each lost Humanity - or 5 Merits dots. It's fair trade, I think. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T12:47:20-07:00","id":553341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/552802-selling-humanity-and-blood-smoke?p=553338#post553338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not normally run Vampire, but I think you could left the rule for price of 5 <b>new</b> XP. That way character could by another Blood Potency dot for each lost Humanity - or 5 Merits dots. It's fair trade, I think. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I dislike the whole idea behind trading Humanity for experience. If you want to play a low humanity character because you think that would make for a more interesting story, just do it, you shouldn't need an xp reward for that. If you only want to play a low humanity character so you can get bonus experience, you're just min-maxing. But if you are going to allow it, 5 new xp is way too much. I mean, you can buy dots of Humanity for 2 xp each, so any more than 2 xp for the drop is a non-choice because you can just buy the humanity back with your bonus xp and still have more left over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T13:17:19-07:00","id":553359,"title":"","content":"I mean, it's all linear now so theoretically if you wanted you could let players buy and sell starting dots in everything with impunity. I don't think the results would be particularly balanced but it sounds like an interesting experiment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T13:20:29-07:00","id":553360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/552802-selling-humanity-and-blood-smoke?p=553341#post553341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dislike the whole idea behind trading Humanity for experience. If you want to play a low humanity character because you think that would make for a more interesting story, just do it, you shouldn't need an xp reward for that. If you only want to play a low humanity character so you can get bonus experience, you're just min-maxing. But if you are going to allow it, 5 new xp is way too much. I mean, you can buy dots of Humanity for 2 xp each, so any more than 2 xp for the drop is a non-choice because you can just buy the humanity back with your bonus xp and still have more left over.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It made a lot more sense in first edition, where buying back Humanity was incredibly, prohibitively, expensive, which made Humanity loss a practically guaranteed step towards losing your character sheet.. But in second, it's very cheap, as you pointed out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-13-2015, 04:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T13:47:37-07:00","id":553372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/552802-selling-humanity-and-blood-smoke?p=553360#post553360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It made a lot more sense in first edition, where buying back Humanity was incredibly, prohibitively, expensive, which made Humanity loss a practically guaranteed step towards losing your character sheet.. But in second, it's very cheap, as you pointed out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, in 1e I still didn't like the idea, but I understood why it was there. With old school exponential xp costs you were actually taking a significant hit by dropping a dot or two of Humanity. But in 2e the costs have been fixed so it's not as big of a drawback and you don't really need compensation for choosing to play a character who has lost some Humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T10:29:42-07:00","id":554558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/552802-selling-humanity-and-blood-smoke?p=553359#post553359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, it's all linear now so theoretically if you wanted you could let players buy and sell starting dots in everything with impunity. I don't think the results would be particularly balanced but it sounds like an interesting experiment.</div> </div> </div> </div>An interesting idea, a new character is worth (12*4=548, 22*2=44, 44+48+7=)99 Experiences, with Vampires getting clan, one dot of blood potency, a touchstone, and 13 extra Experiences. You could easily give players an XP budget and just have them build from there.<br /> <br /> If you don't like starting at integrity/humanity 7 for everyone, give them humanity 1, 12 Experiences, and explain that if they don't buy humanity 7+ they suffer their clan bane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T12:55:53-07:00","id":554710,"title":"","content":"102. You forgot the specialties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T13:39:07-07:00","id":554766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/552802-selling-humanity-and-blood-smoke?p=554710#post554710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">102. You forgot the specialties.</div> </div> </div> </div>I knew I'd forgotten something. Still, at least nWoD 2e makes XP budgets easy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T13:44:14-07:00","id":554789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/552802-selling-humanity-and-blood-smoke?p=554558#post554558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you don't like starting at integrity/humanity 7 for everyone, give them humanity 1, 12 Experiences, and explain that if they don't buy humanity 7+ they suffer their clan bane.</div> </div> </div> </div>I recommend against this, because this way you are rewarding characters for not having to play out their Humanity degeneration. Barring some exceptional Kindred, all vampires will lose some of their Humanity, and it seems weird to give characters, who start at a lower, Humanity bonus XP, while not giving the same amount of XP to characters who lose it during play. That doesn't mean that characters can't begin with a lower Humanity, only that I wouldn't give them XP for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T14:31:45-07:00","id":554875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/552802-selling-humanity-and-blood-smoke?p=554789#post554789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I recommend against this, because this way you are rewarding characters for not having to play out their Humanity degeneration. Barring some exceptional Kindred, all vampires will lose some of their Humanity, and it seems weird to give characters, who start at a lower, Humanity bonus XP, while not giving the same amount of XP to characters who lose it during play. That doesn't mean that characters can't begin with a lower Humanity, only that I wouldn't give them XP for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I agree, it was just a suggestion, as I was working out the XP budgets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T14:36:41-07:00","id":554877,"title":"","content":"It costs 2 xp to buy a point of Humanity so trading one in for 5 is... a very strange way to go. If it is just about giving more experience to start then the rule is unnecessary. There is a rule to allow for giving more experience which costs a player nothing. The trade rule just doesn't have a meaningful place. Having players start with characters that have been around so have more experience and less Humanity is how they did it for the sample story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 06-14-2015, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T06:27:19-07:00","id":559301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/552802-selling-humanity-and-blood-smoke?p=553333#post553333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It isn't a good rule for 2.0. Any way you look at it the trade in would only be 1 exp. You would start out with a clan bane which doesn't normally happen to allow a character to transition into the life and players to have one less thing to worry about at the start. A veteran player might just assume start with the clan bane though. <b>The question is does the player want to start with less Humanity with all that entails or just have more experience to work with at the start. If it is just about experience then talk to the group. If the veteran is going to take a sort of mentor role then they might not mind if that character starts with a little more experience. Otherwise, all the players could go with having been &quot;around the block&quot; and get an additional 5 experience which would generally amount to around 25 in the first edition.</b> Then any that wants to start with Humanity lower than 7 can certainly still do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with the bold. If it's about the players wanting to start with a bit more experience to tailor their characters to their tastes a bit more, then I would just give them an extra 5xp to 10xp and be done with it. I wouldn't worry about any Humanity trade-off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T07:06:03-07:00","id":559342,"title":"","content":"From my experience, this usually comes from the more Game-y type players, who think along the line of &quot;well, i'm gonna lose Humanity anywasy, so if I cash in right now, I also get bonus XP&quot;. This was done away with 2nd ed. Even more so, now that getting Breaking Points provides experience (directly in Beats, and indirectly by conditions(even if you succeed at the roll)) it's more beneficial to stay up. <br /> <br /> Anyways, if a player wanted to drop his humanity, I would probably give him the minimum amount of Beats provided by the fall (that is, assuming he failed his first Breaking Points). And not a single Beat more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T07:31:38-07:00","id":559356,"title":"","content":"So far, that's been my experience with players taking Lair in Beast. Some of the more game-y players have opted for cashing in on the one less chamber at start for 2exp, while the others have been more interested in exploring Lairs as they are. <br /> <br /> I was flat out told that, since they can expand Chambers for free later on, its &quot;dumb&quot; to not start with one less Chamber.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T07:47:04-07:00","id":560818,"title":"","content":"Hi everyone <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I only have experience in 1E but I have read up on 2E (although it was awhile ago). <br /> <br /> The only times I traded starting Humanity for Exp was when it was a rather old vampire that had been in torpor for an incredibly long time. He's done bad things hence the lower humanity, but due to his age (he wasn't staked as soon as he was embraced), he has more exp. I also took a derangement for it though so it made more sense to me. Severe Paranoia about stakes. Anytime he would be near something that could be quickly used as a stake (anything that needed to be broken first didn't count.. He mistrusted them but didn't suffer any penalty towards them. Although he did tend to play with fire to burn everyones wooden tables). Now granted, that could simply fall under the rule &quot;Around the Block&quot; or whatever it was called. Or could of simply been bonus exp for a nifty background (most GM's I've met will do that). Either way, it essentially equated to drop humanity for exp. Just.. Explain it differently! <br /> <br /> On the other note, I do agree that for 2E 5 exp seems way to pricey. Not just due to the fact that Humanity is cheaper to buy, but simply by the level jump. I helped a GM write up a story and antagonists once. Was simply for starting characters at BP1. Now switching it to 2E, that 'boss' that the players had to face had the same amount of exp as a base character + 10 exp. It's almost an entirely different playing field than starting characters. IMO.<br /> <br /> =D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}